<p>Bernard is listed at 6-foot-1 and 206 pounds, with a 9⅞-inch hand and a 30⅜-inch arm. His official combine 40 was <strong>4.48 seconds</strong>. His pre-draft testing also included a 32.5-inch vertical, a 10-foot-5-inch broad jump, a 6.71-second three-cone and a 4.31-second short shuttle.</p>
<p>The scouting reports were consistent. Evaluators liked his route running between the hashes, his hands, his toughness after the catch and his willingness to block. The concerns were physical: not enough long speed to separate vertically, limited wiggle in tight spaces, and short arms for contested catches. Bleacher Report's pre-draft comparison was Jarvis Landry, a slot receiver who built a long career on routes and hands rather than burst.</p>
