<h2>The Record Game</h2>
<p>Bernard barely played early in the season in a crowded receiver room. Injuries opened the door: with Roman Wilson on injured reserve and other receivers out, he moved into a full-time role alongside DK Metcalf. The results came fast.</p>
<div class="table-scroll"><table class="data-table">
<thead>
<tr><th>Game</th><th>Catches / Targets</th><th>Yards</th><th>TD</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Week 5 vs Colts (first start)</td><td>6 / 9</td><td>80</td><td>0</td></tr>
<tr class="highlight"><td>Week 6 at Buccaneers (OT win)</td><td>11 / 12</td><td>87</td><td>1</td></tr>
<tr><td>Season through Week 6</td><td>24 catches</td><td>227</td><td>1</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>His 11 catches in the 26-19 overtime win topped JuJu Smith-Schuster's Steelers rookie record of 9 from 2017, and his first career touchdown was the game-winner. Afterward, Aaron Rodgers said Bernard's confidence is starting to match his potential.</p>
<h2>Why the Slot Is the Right Fit for His Profile</h2>
<p>The details of the Week 6 game explain the record. Bernard lined up in the slot on 61% of his snaps, up from 44% over the first five weeks. He ran a team-high 54 routes, drew a 28% target share and averaged 7.9 yards per catch. Those are short, quick, high-volume targets, exactly the job his scouting report described.</p>
<p>A slot receiver rarely needs to run a full 40 yards in a straight line. The first 10 yards, the break at the top of the route and the ability to catch in traffic decide most plays. That's why his three-cone (6.71) and short shuttle (4.31) are the more relevant numbers for this role. Both drills measure how quickly an athlete can stop, change direction and re-accelerate, which is what separation from a slot defender actually requires.</p>
<div class="callout">
<div class="callout-icon">🏋️</div>
<div class="callout-text"><strong>Training takeaway:</strong> If you're a receiver who doesn't run a 4.3, Bernard is the template. Acceleration over the first 10 yards and clean change of direction can be trained more directly than top speed. Our guide on <a href="/how-to-run-faster-40-yard-dash">how to run a faster 40</a> covers the start and drive phase, which is where most short routes are won.</div>
</div>
<h2>Next Up: Paris</h2>
<p>Pittsburgh (4-2) faces New Orleans in Paris in Week 7, the first NFL game ever played in the French capital. With the receiver room still thin, Bernard should keep his slot role opposite Metcalf. Two games is a small sample, but it's already more production than the fastest receivers in his class have managed.</p>
